\newlabel{sub@fig:sign_oracle_synth}{{a}{38}{Synthetic dataset (top 10 features by mean $D_{\text {oracle}}$). Asymmetric rows are near-zero; Causal and Flow concentrate oracle sign disagreement on X27, X36, and X34, a distinct set from the magnitude leaders (X24, X33, X47), reflecting that near-zero attributions on these features are inverted by relatively small graph-induced shifts}{figure.caption.29}{}}
\newlabel{fig:sign_oracle_sachs}{{12b}{38}{Sachs dataset (top 10 features by mean $D_{\text {oracle}}$). Sign disagreement concentrates on plc, pkc, and pip2; only pkc overlaps with the magnitude heatmap leaders, confirming that sign-flip-vulnerable features are those whose oracle attributions sit close to zero, not the high-magnitude nodes}{figure.caption.29}{}}
